# Local run script carrying the ingest key and the GitHub client id. Useful to
# keep, must never be committed — see ingest/SETUP.md.
run-configured.sh
# Per-machine build secret (the telemetry ingest key) — read by app/scripts/build-config.mjs.
app/.flow-build.local.json

# Project knowledge stays local — never committed, never pushed (2026-10-13).
# `flow/` holds the discoveries, plans, brainstorms, reviews and the brain;
# `blueprint-territory/` is an older set of the same. 242 files were untracked
# with `git rm -r --cached`, so every file is still on disk and the app still
# reads them — git simply stops carrying them.
#
# These two lines deliberately sit OUTSIDE the managed `>>> plan-flow` block
# above, which was written for "shared" mode and still lists individual flow/
# paths. Anything regenerating that block must not undo these.
#
# LEADING SLASH, BECAUSE `flow/` MATCHES AT ANY DEPTH. Unanchored, it also
# ignored app/src/main/flow/ and app/src/renderer/flow/ — 28 source files. They
# were tracked before the rule existed, so this repo never noticed; a fresh
# clone did, and `git add` there silently dropped all 28. The rule is about the
# knowledge folder at the root, so it says the root.
/flow/
/blueprint-territory/

# Build output and e2e debug screenshots stay local (2026-10-14).
#
# `app/out/` is the electron-vite bundle. It was tracked, and its committed copy
# matched no build that existed on disk — a stale bundle that still carried
# pre-scrub identifiers long after the sources were cleaned. Build output is
# regenerated by `npm run build`; nothing should carry it in git.
#
# `__screens/` holds Playwright screenshots. Nothing reads them back — there is
# not one snapshot comparison in the suite; the specs only ever WRITE there, as
# debug evidence. The committed images showed real project names, real internal
# architecture read off a live checkout, and the author's login and hostname in
# the terminal panel, which is visible by default. Pixels cannot be grepped, so
# no text scan would ever have found any of it. The specs recreate the folder on
# the next run.
app/out/
app/e2e/__screens/
app/e2e/ux/__screens/

# Third-party skill packs installed by the skills manager, plus its lockfile.
# `.agents/skills/planflow-workflow/` is this repo's OWN guidance for native
# Codex (de2cd80f) and stays tracked; everything else under `skills/` arrived
# from a registry, is reinstallable, and was swept into a commit by `git add -A`
# without anybody choosing to publish it.
.agents/skills/*
!.agents/skills/planflow-workflow/
skills-lock.json

# Playwright's own run output. Every run writes it; nothing reads it back, and
# a traces/screenshots folder is exactly the kind of thing `git add -A` sweeps
# into a commit unnoticed.
app/e2e/results/
